      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T06:05:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "scope, deviceId (now chipId), platformId, skuId, chipletId and moduleId identify where the event was generated. Their values have different meanings on different products, so they can\u0027t be described by a single enum, and the tools that consume these records need them to identify a failure. They are kept as plain numbers, similar to the source identifiers in other OEM sections, such as Ampere (typeId, subTypeId, instanceId) and NVIDIA Event (SocketNum, chipId):\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libcper/blob/3a81ccbd9dc7ae9cce4b3082dd60928b9fe3163e/sections/cper-section-ampere.c#L38-L40\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libcper/blob/3a81ccbd9dc7ae9cce4b3082dd60928b9fe3163e/sections/cper-section-nvidia-events.c#L509-L536\n\nPlease let me know if you have other suggestions.",
