      "lineNbr": 85,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002581
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T06:05:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review. I\u0027d like to keep these two. detailFormatId identifies the format of eventDetailRaw, and detailLength gives the length of the data in it. detailLength is 48 for all current formats, and is there so future formats can use variable-length payloads. This is similar to NVIDIA Event, which also publishes dataFormatType and dataSize alongside its payload:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libcper/blob/3a81ccbd9dc7ae9cce4b3082dd60928b9fe3163e/sections/cper-section-nvidia-events.c#L2010-L2014\nPlease let me know if you have other suggestions.",
      "parentUuid": "f522ee67_7bdd2825",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 85,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "418a8427cbcecdb2c6e86e970bca70d146a0798f",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
