      "lineNbr": 85,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000153
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T21:00:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e detailLength is 48 for all current formats, and is there so future formats can use variable-length payloads\n\nAnd when those formats come, nothing should be using the length or type as a branch, they will use the new format schema and properties to determine that.\n\nOn the Nvidia ones, you\u0027re right, I missed that in a review.  If you look into the review, you will find I made the exact same comment on the Nvidia review as i\u0027m making here.  I will get those removed.\n\n\nOverall, I would like libcper to move to a human and data facing decode, not an internal description of the format itself.  Including \"length\" moves backwards, and adds things to the decode that have no use.",
      "parentUuid": "26725dd2_62630dd2",
      "range": {
